        "response": {
          "bodySize": 264369,
          "content": {
            "mimeType": "text/html; charset=utf-8",
            "size": 264369,
            "text": "\r\n\r\n<!DOCTYPE html>\r\n<!--[if lt IE 7]> \t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie6 lte9 lte8 lte7 \">\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if IE 7]>\t\t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie7 lte9 lte8 lte7 \">\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if IE 8]>\t\t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie8 lte9 lte8 \">\t\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if IE 9]>\t\t\t\t\t<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\" class=\"ie ie9 lte9 \">\t\t\t\t<![endif]-->\r\n<!--[if (gt IE 9)|!(IE)]><!-->\r\n<html xmlns=\"http://www.w3.org/1999/xhtml\" xml:lang=\"en\" lang=\"en\">\r\n<!--<![endif]-->\r\n<head id=\"Head1\"><title>\r\n\tMARGINAL FILM SESSION III: Black and Queer Cinema - WED 29 OCT  –  6:30 PM Tickets | 29 Oct @ SOAS University of London, London | Pay What You Can to £11 | OutSavvy\r\n</title>\r\n\r\n    <script type=\"text/javascript\">\r\n        window.dataLayer = window.dataLayer || [];\r\n\r\n        function gtag() { dataLayer.push(arguments); }\r\n\r\n        if (window.location.hash ? window.location.hash == '#cs-scan' : false) {\r\n            gtag(\"consent\", \"default\", { ad_storage: \"granted\", ad_user_data: \"granted\", ad_personalization: \"granted\", analytics_storage: \"granted\", functionality_storage: \"granted\", personalization_storage: \"granted\", security_storage: \"granted\", wait_for_update: 500 });\r\n        }\r\n        else {\r\n            gtag(\"consent\", \"default\", {\r\n                ad_storage: \"denied\",\r\n                ad_user_data: \"denied\",\r\n                ad_personalization: \"denied\",\r\n                analytics_storage: \"denied\",\r\n                functionality_storage: \"granted\",\r\n                personalization_storage: \"granted\",\r\n                security_storage: \"granted\",\r\n                wait_for_update: 500,\r\n            });\r\n        }\r\n\r\n        gtag(\"set\", \"ads_data_redaction\", true);\r\n\r\n        gtag(\"set\", \"developer_id.dZTlmZj\", true);\r\n    </script>\r\n\r\n    <script src=\"https://consent.studio/outsavvy.com/banner.js\"></script>\r\n\r\n    <link rel=\"stylesheet\" type=\"text/css\" href=\"/combres.axd/siteCss/48b1003e3f996725d29958c6407c7628d895b6c59423ce86809d490268602a4108a2f455d42039841e6a37763c49dbae39bb99ea85f2d7ab12be682be45831a8/\"/><script type=\"text/javascript\" src=\"/combres.axd/siteJs/4ea27d3d3dfdcea6aa2256650964498a5d720acb896b38d1bcbc2a81e57470911dd600418c7f575901cd7b3741c1b3a433126ce5ab0a56f134539cecb5333ade/\"></script>\r\n\r\n    <meta name=\"Priority\" content=\"1.0\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"ChangeFrequency\" content=\"daily\" />\r\n\r\n    <meta http-equiv=\"last-modified\" name=\"LastModified\" content=\"2025-10-28\" />\r\n\r\n    \r\n    <meta name=\"robots\" content=\"index, follow\" />\r\n    \r\n\r\n    <meta property=\"og:description\" content=\" &#128467; Wednesday 29th October | 7pm start (doors 6.30pm)&#128205;  SOAS University of London (10 Thornhaugh Street London WC1H 0XG)  &#128270; Room: KLT  (Khalili Lecture Theatre)Rating: Suitable for ages 16+ Duration: 1 hour 35 minutesTo be followed with a Q&amp;amp;A session with Uilton Oliveira, the Festival Curator from BrazilAll films are in Brazilian Portuguese with English subtitles. Programme:5 short films that explore Black, trans, and queer experiences — tracing paths of memory, love, and ancestral power from the dancefloors of Rio to Candombl&#233; terreiros. 1. Voll&#250;pya Documentary, 21’ min, 16+, 2024. Directed by &#201;ri Sarmet and Jocimar Dias Jr.In a post-apocalyptic future, an intergalactic explorer lands in an abandoned museum in search of vestiges of their ancestors and ends up teleported to the dance floor of a “GLS” (Gay, Lesbian and Sympathizer) nightclub in Niter&#243;i, Rio de Janeiro.  Built from video archives, photographs, and audio testimonies, this short film mixes science fiction and documentary to present a sensitive and unique perspective on Brazilian queer nightlife in the 1990s.2. Sangria  Fiction, 23’ min, 14+, 2024. Directed by Rudyeri Ribeiro.As he’s about to close up the bar where he works, Rubens agrees to serve one last customer — the mysterious Zion.3. Um dia de Neg&#227;o – A Black Man’s DayDocumentary, 7’ min, 14+, 2024. Directed by Rebeca Carmo and Analu. Three Black trans men confront manifestations of their unconscious as  they go about their daily lives in the neighborhood of Nordeste de Amaralina.  Each encounter mirrors their inner struggles and the pressures of a society that  demands a rigid form of masculinity. Through these experiences, they reflect on  what it means to embrace a healthier freer masculinity, free from stereotypes.  4. L&#237;rios  – LiliesFiction, 20’ min, 14+, 2025. Directed by Lupe Capitani.Gabriel and Rita, a trans girl, have been friends since childhood. But a weekend trip to Chapada dos Guimar&#227;es may reveal the romance they’ve long tried to deny.5. In - Nil&#232; Documentary, 24’ min, All Ages, 2025. Directed by Jener Mendes and Deko Alves. An experimental mini-doc that portrays the lives, stories, and daily routines of three trans M&#227;es de Santo of Candombl&#233;: Ana Vit&#243;ria de Oy&#225;, Alana de Carvalho, and Thiffany Odara. Through their narratives and a poetic exploration, the film reveals their trajectories of resistance and leadership, showing how they transform their terreiros into spaces of care, power, and reaffirmation. Between the sacred and the everyday, In-Nil&#232; invites viewers to reflect on the intersection of faith, identity, and struggle - celebrating these voices that make their terreiros territories of freedom, diversity, and belonging. Sinopse em portugu&#234;sVoll&#250;pya (RJ)Document&#225;rio, 21′, 16 anos, 2024. Dire&#231;&#227;o: &#201;ri Sarmet e Jocimar Dias Jr.Legenda Descritiva, Audiodescri&#231;&#227;o e Libras.Num futuro p&#243;s-apocal&#237;ptico, um explorador intergal&#225;ctico aterrissa em um museu abandonado em busca de vest&#237;gios de seus antepassados e acaba sendo teletransportado para a pista de dan&#231;a de uma boate “GLS” em Niter&#243;i, Rio de Janeiro. Misturando fic&#231;&#227;o cient&#237;fica e document&#225;rio, este curta-metragem elaborado a partir de arquivos de v&#237;deo, fotografias e depoimentos de &#225;udio apresenta uma perspectiva sens&#237;vel e &#250;nica sobre a vida noturna queer brasileira nos anos 1990.Sangria (PA)Fic&#231;&#227;o, 23′, 14 anos, 2024. Dire&#231;&#227;o: Rudyeri Ribeiro.Legenda Descritiva, Audiodescri&#231;&#227;o e Libras.Prestes a encerrar o expediente do bar em que trabalha, Rubens aceita atender um &#250;ltimo cliente: o misterioso Zion.Um dia de Neg&#227;o (BA)Document&#225;rio, 07′, 14 anos, 2024. Dire&#231;&#227;o: Rebeca Carmo e Analu.Legenda em Portugu&#234;s.Tr&#234;s homens trans negros enfrentam manifesta&#231;&#245;es de seus inconscientes enquanto vivem suas rotinas no Nordeste de Amaralina. Cada encontro reflete suas lutas internas e as press&#245;es de uma sociedade que exige uma masculinidade r&#237;gida. Em meio a essas experi&#234;ncias, eles compartilham reflex&#245;es sobre as expectativas de viver uma masculinidade mais saud&#225;vel e livre de estere&#243;tipos.L&#237;rios (MT)Fic&#231;&#227;o, 20′, 14 anos, 2025. Dire&#231;&#227;o: Lupe Capitani.Libras.Gabriel e Rita, uma garota trans, s&#227;o amigos desde a inf&#226;ncia. Mas uma viagem de fim de semana para Chapada dos Guimar&#227;es pode revelar o romance que eles insistem em negar.In – Nil&#232; (BA)Document&#225;rio, 24′, Livre, 2025. Dire&#231;&#227;o: Jener Mendes e Deko Alves.Legenda Descritiva.In-Nil&#232; &#233; um mini-doc experimental que retrata a vida, a hist&#243;ria e o cotidiano de tr&#234;s m&#227;es de santo trans do candombl&#233;: Ana Vit&#243;ria de Oy&#225;, Alana de Carvalho e Thiffany Odara. Por meio de suas narrativas em uma explora&#231;&#227;o po&#233;tica, o filme revela suas trajet&#243;rias de resist&#234;ncia e lideran&#231;a, evidenciando como elas transformam seus terreiros em espa&#231;os de acolhimento, poder e reafirma&#231;&#227;o. Entre o sagrado e o cotidiano, In-Nil&#232; convida o p&#250;blico a refletir sobre a interse&#231;&#227;o entre f&#233;, identidade e luta, celebrando essas vozes que fazem de seus terreiros territ&#243;rios de liberdade, diversidade e pertencimento. \" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:locale\" content=\"en_GB\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:locale:alternate\" content=\"en_US\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:site_name\" content=\"OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:type\" content=\"website\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:title\" content=\"MARGINAL FILM SESSION III: Black and Queer Cinema - WED 29 OCT  –  6:30 PM Tickets - London - OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:url\" content=\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/30749/marginal-film-session-iii-black-and-queer-cinema-wed-29-oct-630-pm\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image:type\" content=\"image/jpg\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image:width\" content=\"1200\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image:height\" content=\"584\" />\r\n    <meta property=\"og:image\" content=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/events/ff038bea-9e8e-40cd-9279-90edae25e381.png\" />\r\n\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:card\" content=\"summary_large_image\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:site\" content=\"@OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:title\" content=\"MARGINAL FILM SESSION III: Black and Queer Cinema - WED 29 OCT  –  6:30 PM Tickets - London - OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:url\" content=\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/30749/marginal-film-session-iii-black-and-queer-cinema-wed-29-oct-630-pm\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:app:name:iphone\" content=\"OutSavvy\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:app:id:iphone\" content=\"722344276\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:image\" content=\"https://cdn.outsavvy.com/events/ff038bea-9e8e-40cd-9279-90edae25e381.png?width=1200\" />\r\n    <meta name=\"twitter:description\" content=\" &#128467; Wednesday 29th October | 7pm start (doors 6.30pm)&#128205;  SOAS University of London (10 Thornhaugh Street London WC1H 0XG)  &#128270; Room: KLT  (Khalili Lecture Theatre)Rating: Suitable for ages 16+ Duration: 1 hour 35 minutesTo be followed with a Q&amp;amp;A session with Uilton Oliveira, the Festival Curator from BrazilAll films are in Brazilian Portuguese with English subtitles. Programme:5 short films that explore Black, trans, and queer experiences — tracing paths of memory, love, and ancestral power from the dancefloors of Rio to Candombl&#233; terreiros. 1. Voll&#250;pya Documentary, 21’ min, 16+, 2024. Directed by &#201;ri Sarmet and Jocimar Dias Jr.In a post-apocalyptic future, an intergalactic explorer lands in an abandoned museum in search of vestiges of their ancestors and ends up teleported to the dance floor of a “GLS” (Gay, Lesbian and Sympathizer) nightclub in Niter&#243;i, Rio de Janeiro.  Built from video archives, photographs, and audio testimonies, this short film mixes science fiction and documentary to present a sensitive and unique perspective on Brazilian queer nightlife in the 1990s.2. Sangria  Fiction, 23’ min, 14+, 2024. Directed by Rudyeri Ribeiro.As he’s about to close up the bar where he works, Rubens agrees to serve one last customer — the mysterious Zion.3. Um dia de Neg&#227;o – A Black Man’s DayDocumentary, 7’ min, 14+, 2024. Directed by Rebeca Carmo and Analu. Three Black trans men confront manifestations of their unconscious as  they go about their daily lives in the neighborhood of Nordeste de Amaralina.  Each encounter mirrors their inner struggles and the pressures of a society that  demands a rigid form of masculinity. Through these experiences, they reflect on  what it means to embrace a healthier freer masculinity, free from stereotypes.  4. L&#237;rios  – LiliesFiction, 20’ min, 14+, 2025. Directed by Lupe Capitani.Gabriel and Rita, a trans girl, have been friends since childhood. But a weekend trip to Chapada dos Guimar&#227;es may reveal the romance they’ve long tried to deny.5. In - Nil&#232; Documentary, 24’ min, All Ages, 2025. Directed by Jener Mendes and Deko Alves. An experimental mini-doc that portrays the lives, stories, and daily routines of three trans M&#227;es de Santo of Candombl&#233;: Ana Vit&#243;ria de Oy&#225;, Alana de Carvalho, and Thiffany Odara. Through their narratives and a poetic exploration, the film reveals their trajectories of resistance and leadership, showing how they transform their terreiros into spaces of care, power, and reaffirmation. Between the sacred and the everyday, In-Nil&#232; invites viewers to reflect on the intersection of faith, identity, and struggle - celebrating these voices that make their terreiros territories of freedom, diversity, and belonging. Sinopse em portugu&#234;sVoll&#250;pya (RJ)Document&#225;rio, 21′, 16 anos, 2024. Dire&#231;&#227;o: &#201;ri Sarmet e Jocimar Dias Jr.Legenda Descritiva, Audiodescri&#231;&#227;o e Libras.Num futuro p&#243;s-apocal&#237;ptico, um explorador intergal&#225;ctico aterrissa em um museu abandonado em busca de vest&#237;gios de seus antepassados e acaba sendo teletransportado para a pista de dan&#231;a de uma boate “GLS” em Niter&#243;i, Rio de Janeiro. Misturando fic&#231;&#227;o cient&#237;fica e document&#225;rio, este curta-metragem elaborado a partir de arquivos de v&#237;deo, fotografias e depoimentos de &#225;udio apresenta uma perspectiva sens&#237;vel e &#250;nica sobre a vida noturna queer brasileira nos anos 1990.Sangria (PA)Fic&#231;&#227;o, 23′, 14 anos, 2024. Dire&#231;&#227;o: Rudyeri Ribeiro.Legenda Descritiva, Audiodescri&#231;&#227;o e Libras.Prestes a encerrar o expediente do bar em que trabalha, Rubens aceita atender um &#250;ltimo cliente: o misterioso Zion.Um dia de Neg&#227;o (BA)Document&#225;rio, 07′, 14 anos, 2024. Dire&#231;&#227;o: Rebeca Carmo e Analu.Legenda em Portugu&#234;s.Tr&#234;s homens trans negros enfrentam manifesta&#231;&#245;es de seus inconscientes enquanto vivem suas rotinas no Nordeste de Amaralina. Cada encontro reflete suas lutas internas e as press&#245;es de uma sociedade que exige uma masculinidade r&#237;gida. Em meio a essas experi&#234;ncias, eles compartilham reflex&#245;es sobre as expectativas de viver uma masculinidade mais saud&#225;vel e livre de estere&#243;tipos.L&#237;rios (MT)Fic&#231;&#227;o, 20′, 14 anos, 2025. Dire&#231;&#227;o: Lupe Capitani.Libras.Gabriel e Rita, uma garota trans, s&#227;o amigos desde a inf&#226;ncia. Mas uma viagem de fim de semana para Chapada dos Guimar&#227;es pode revelar o romance que eles insistem em negar.In – Nil&#232; (BA)Document&#225;rio, 24′, Livre, 2025. Dire&#231;&#227;o: Jener Mendes e Deko Alves.Legenda Descritiva.In-Nil&#232; &#233; um mini-doc experimental que retrata a vida, a hist&#243;ria e o cotidiano de tr&#234;s m&#227;es de santo trans do candombl&#233;: Ana Vit&#243;ria de Oy&#225;, Alana de Carvalho e Thiffany Odara. Por meio de suas narrativas em uma explora&#231;&#227;o po&#233;tica, o filme revela suas trajet&#243;rias de resist&#234;ncia e lideran&#231;a, evidenciando como elas transformam seus terreiros em espa&#231;os de acolhimento, poder e reafirma&#231;&#227;o. Entre o sagrado e o cotidiano, In-Nil&#232; convida o p&#250;blico a refletir sobre a interse&#231;&#227;o entre f&#233;, identidade e luta, celebrando essas vozes que fazem de seus terreiros territ&#243;rios de liberdade, diversidade e pertencimento. \" />\r\n\r\n    <link rel=\"canonical\" href=\"https://www.outsavvy.com/event/30749/marginal-film-session-iii-black-and-queer-cinema-wed-29-oct-630-pm\" />\r\n\r\n    <meta name=\"description\" content=\"OutSavvy | MARGINAL FILM SESSION III: Black and Queer Cinema - WED 29 OCT  –  6:30 PM | Wednesday 29th October 2025 @ SOAS University of London | Pay What You Can to £11 | Find event and ticket information for